## 5. Compliance

| ID | Requirement | Testable Criterion |
|----|-------------|-------------------|
| CXC-GEST-C1 | 4-way classification | Down→move→up over threshold classifies as up/down/left/right correctly; sub-threshold stays tap/pan |
| CXC-GEST-C2 | No regression | Tap, long-press, and pan (M1) still work unchanged alongside swipe |
| CXC-GEST-C3 | Bus event | A recognized swipe publishes direction + target to a namespace |
| CXC-GEST-C4 | Declarative reaction | A config maps a swipe to a behavior/command via [SPEC:CXC-BIND] and it fires |
| CXC-GEST-C5 | Intelligence parity | An injected swipe event drives the surface identically to a physical swipe |
| CXC-GEST-C6 | Touch hardware | Swipe recognizes on the CYD XPT2046 panel with the tuned thresholds |
| CXC-GEST-C7 | Gesture producer | A `gestures:` block publishes a semantic bus state a [CXC-BIND-STATES] selector consumes; an Intelligence publishing the same namespace produces the IDENTICAL transition; `@pointer` resolves to surface coords; inline code refused |

